==Usage== <!--T:7-->

<!--T:8-->
# Select a loop of 3 connected [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly4.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlPoly4|ControlPoly4]] sequentially in counter-clockwise direction (looking from the "outer side" of the surface to be created) in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# There are several ways to invoke the command.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_ControlGrid44_Rotate.svg|16px]] ControlGrid44_Rotate}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Silk → [[Image:Silk_ControlGrid44_Rotate.svg|16px]] ControlGrid44_Rotate}} option from the menu.
# A 4x4 rotate grid, a '''ControlGrid44_3_Rotate''' object, is created.

==Notes== <!--T:20-->

<!--T:21-->
* This tool produces a "triangle" surface that "rotates" from the first edge selected to the third, following along the second edge. Order is "left, bottom, right," with the rotational pivot at the "top" corner.
* Typical use is to merge a set of surfaces to a point (such as closing a tube). Also used to interface with spheres and ellipsoids.
* This is a degenerate grid (one edge collapsed to a point) that results in a "revolve"-like surface. Produces true spheres from arc polys, true ellipsoids from ellipse-arc polys, but also accepts non-arc polys.
* Surface tangency across multiple grids can be achieved automatically from well-prepared arcs of circles and ellipses, but using general curves as input does not have an easily predictable outcome, and additional blending may be required.
* Although degenerate, this grid is the correct way to interface with spheres, since it does not introduce additional collapsed edges — in this particular case, the NURBS degeneracy is not a flaw at all, but a standard CAD construct.
* A four-sided version able to create true tori (and sphere strips) is planned, but not yet ready.

== Properties == <!--T:9-->

<!--T:10-->
See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

<!--T:11-->
A 4x4 rotate grid, a '''ControlGrid44_3_Rotate''' object, is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

=== Data === <!--T:12-->

<!--T:13-->
{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

<!--T:14-->
* {{PropertyData|Poly0|Link}}: First control polygon.
* {{PropertyData|Poly1|Link}}: Second control polygon.
* {{PropertyData|Poly2|Link}}: Third control polygon.
* {{PropertyData|reverse|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the parameter direction.
* {{PropertyData|tolerance|Float}}: Default is {{value|1e-06}}. Point-to-point connection tolerance for the 3 corners.

<!--T:15-->
{{Properties_Title|C2 - Outputs}}

<!--T:16-->
* {{PropertyData|Legs|Part::PropertyGeometryList}}: Control segments.
* {{PropertyData|Poles|VectorList}}: Poles.
* {{PropertyData|Weights|FloatList}}: Weights.

<!--T:17-->
{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

<!--T:18-->
* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|ControlGrid44_3_Rotate}}. The workbench class used to create this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


